# C2-S15 Fragment Two, C2-S16 Flight 707, C2-S17 Seraphina's commitment.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2530–2610.
# Scene: scenes/chapter2/seraphina_choice.tscn.
# S17 is NOT a recruit button: Seraphina decides from how Kaelen has behaved
# and whether the city can spare her. The scene sets ch2_city_stable first;
# seraphina_trust_low comes from the trust events (DialogueManager).

# C2-S15 — the second fragment, and a worse memory.
~ fragment
do touch_fragment
System: SOURCE AUTHORIZATION: TWO OF SEVEN.
do memory_flash
Colleague: Seven signatures is too slow in an emergency.
Kaelen (Memory): That's exactly when you want it slow.
Colleague: Until somebody's unconscious and can't sign.
# Past Kaelen hesitates. That's the whole memory: him hesitating.
do flash_ends
do fragment_acquired 2
Seraphina: You had that look again. Like a passenger who's just heard the engines change.
Kaelen: Another memory. Give me a second, it's still arriving.
Seraphina: Yours?
Kaelen: Mine. Someone asked me a question and I didn't answer it fast enough.
Seraphina: A bad one?
Kaelen: I don't know yet. It's hard to judge a room you're still standing in.
# She studies him the way she'd study a passenger who says he's fine.
Seraphina: Tell me when you do.
set ch2_seraphina_tell_me

# C2-S16 — the upper wall. No music for the first part.
~ wall
do upper_wall
Seraphina: I remember the plane.
Kaelen: More than I do. I've got pieces. A sound, a colour, all in the wrong order.
Seraphina: I wish I didn't. I still count the room before I can sleep.
Kaelen: I remember rain on a window. That's one of my pieces.
Seraphina: There was rain.
Kaelen: Not on the plane, though. An airport window, before we boarded.
Seraphina: You had a laptop open.
# He looks at her.
Seraphina: You were typing all through boarding. You didn't look up once.
Kaelen: Was I? ...Yes. Fixing something nobody had asked me to fix.
Seraphina: I told you to close it for takeoff.
Kaelen: Did I close it?
Seraphina: Eventually. The second time I asked, in the voice I save for people who don't listen.
# She smiles, once.
Seraphina: You looked annoyed.
Kaelen: I probably was. Did I at least say thank you?
Seraphina: No. You held up one finger at me, like I was a waiter. I didn't like you.
Kaelen: So far I'm rude, slow and difficult. Tell me there's a better part coming.
Seraphina: Then we crashed.
do pause 1.5
Seraphina: I counted people until I couldn't.
[if seraphina_trust_high and not ch2_seraphina_186_told] Seraphina: One hundred and eighty-six. That's where I stopped.
Kaelen: I'm— I should have—
Seraphina: For what?
Kaelen: ...I don't know.
Seraphina: Then stop. Don't apologise for the crash unless you remember causing it.

# C2-S17 — she decides.
~ commitment
[if seraphina_trust_low] => rejected
[if not ch2_city_stable] => stays
=> recruited

~ recruited
Seraphina: Brask can hold the city.
Brask: Commander. I'd prefer that in a report.
Seraphina: You'll get one. It'll say the same thing, with more commas.
Seraphina: I'm going with Kaelen.
Brask: That wasn't a request, was it.
Seraphina: No. The shift lists are on my desk, every name. I'm sorry, Brask.
set ch2_seraphina_recruited

~ stays
Seraphina: I can't leave. Not while there are people here I haven't counted twice.
Kaelen: I understand. It's yours.
Seraphina: Do you? You've never had a city.
Kaelen: No. But I've got a list of names I'm trying to keep, and it keeps getting longer.
set ch2_seraphina_stayed

~ rejected
Seraphina: I believe your problem is real, Kaelen. I'm saying that first, so you hear it.
Seraphina: I don't believe following you is the same thing as solving it.
set ch2_seraphina_rejected
